[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2e69b893-dca1-5a00-a0a1-d673b040380f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e69b893-dca1-5a00-a0a1-d673b040380f" :question/id #uuid "2e69b893-dca1-5a00-a0a1-d673b040380f" :question/math-academy-id "q-44983" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the geometric sequence given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3{a}_{n}}{5},\\,\\,{a}_{1}=\\frac{10}{3},\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nSo, we must determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common ratio $r.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=\\frac{10}{3}.$ To find the common ratio, we compare the given sequence with the general recursive formula for a geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the above, we see that $r=-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{1}=\\frac{10}{3}$ and $r=-\\frac{3}{5}$ into the formula for the $n$th term, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify further by manipulating the exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{-1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10\\cdot 5}{3\\cdot 3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =-\\frac{50}{9}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{50}{9}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7ee0f6b8-65be-5837-90b0-536ef0f796f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7ee0f6b8-65be-5837-90b0-536ef0f796f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee0f6b8-65be-5837-90b0-536ef0f796f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-89d2e657-a6a8-59f6-8532-79d2b8c65bf3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" "answer-039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" "answer-89d2e657-a6a8-59f6-8532-79d2b8c65bf3" "answer-af390c1b-5127-52ed-92c3-72c04d0ab64c" "answer-6cb8b6d5-6d81-50d2-85a0-0755a8afe296"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" :answer/id #uuid "897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-2\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" :answer/id #uuid "039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89d2e657-a6a8-59f6-8532-79d2b8c65bf3" :answer/id #uuid "89d2e657-a6a8-59f6-8532-79d2b8c65bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\frac{50}{9}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af390c1b-5127-52ed-92c3-72c04d0ab64c" :answer/id #uuid "af390c1b-5127-52ed-92c3-72c04d0ab64c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=2\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cb8b6d5-6d81-50d2-85a0-0755a8afe296" :answer/id #uuid "6cb8b6d5-6d81-50d2-85a0-0755a8afe296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133935 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-072376b1-6413-51af-98f6-95587e3acbf3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-072376b1-6413-51af-98f6-95587e3acbf3" :question/id #uuid "072376b1-6413-51af-98f6-95587e3acbf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-44986" :question/problem "What is the explicit formula for the $n$th term of the geometric sequence given by\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=\\frac{f(n)}{2},\\,\\,f(1)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\,n\\ge 1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite our recursive formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1)=\\frac{f(n)}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}f(n)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)\\cdot {r}^{n-1},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nSo, we must determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common ratio $r.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ To find the common ratio, we compare the given sequence with the general recursive formula for a geometric sequence:\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=r\\cdot f(n)\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the above, we see that $r=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the formula for the $n$th term, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify further by manipulating the exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9947e7a8-c30a-59fb-977d-989052168899"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9947e7a8-c30a-59fb-977d-989052168899" :answer-field/id #uuid "9947e7a8-c30a-59fb-977d-989052168899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ca374ed-64c4-537e-9df7-38e602f55fd2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-955d3208-98c9-5cd1-a334-320a252d84ee" "answer-2ca374ed-64c4-537e-9df7-38e602f55fd2" "answer-679a841f-b122-5f85-a654-2b11ecc33553" "answer-4a4e66bc-7a14-5aba-9a6a-a17f030fcf54" "answer-4301ea6f-1c49-5f63-a937-a2c2069919c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-955d3208-98c9-5cd1-a334-320a252d84ee" :answer/id #uuid "955d3208-98c9-5cd1-a334-320a252d84ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{n-1}},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ca374ed-64c4-537e-9df7-38e602f55fd2" :answer/id #uuid "2ca374ed-64c4-537e-9df7-38e602f55fd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{n}},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-679a841f-b122-5f85-a654-2b11ecc33553" :answer/id #uuid "679a841f-b122-5f85-a654-2b11ecc33553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{1}{{4}^{n}},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a4e66bc-7a14-5aba-9a6a-a17f030fcf54" :answer/id #uuid "4a4e66bc-7a14-5aba-9a6a-a17f030fcf54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)={2}^{n-1},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4301ea6f-1c49-5f63-a937-a2c2069919c4" :answer/id #uuid "4301ea6f-1c49-5f63-a937-a2c2069919c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)={2}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-715d8ed0-87e8-5b42-a40f-879649ce1b0d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-715d8ed0-87e8-5b42-a40f-879649ce1b0d" :question/id #uuid "715d8ed0-87e8-5b42-a40f-879649ce1b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-44995" :question/problem "The formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is $f(n)=3\\cdot {2}^{n+1}$ for $n\\ge 1.$  What is the recursive formula for this sequence?" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=r\\cdot f(n).\n$$\n\nTo complete the formula, we must determine the common ratio $r$ and state the first term ${a}_{1}.$ The first two terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =3\\cdot {2}^{1+1}=3\\cdot 4=12, \\\\ f(2) & =3\\cdot {2}^{2+1}=3\\cdot 8=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{24}{12}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula for the geometric  sequence is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=2f(n),\\,f(1)=12,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66bae46d-9a2a-5dcb-a638-46a59f8b52be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66bae46d-9a2a-5dcb-a638-46a59f8b52be" :answer-field/id #uuid "66bae46d-9a2a-5dcb-a638-46a59f8b52be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b933277-b836-55ae-9b21-a1a99505fdc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b933277-b836-55ae-9b21-a1a99505fdc8" "answer-9c6698c3-0e55-55e1-a6c5-bc756af04932" "answer-71f17afc-b6a1-50e6-8314-cf085641ebf2" "answer-227897ea-9dd1-5b96-9c06-008a8a2d99f1" "answer-3a562547-fbeb-5f3b-853f-ddbd84961e5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b933277-b836-55ae-9b21-a1a99505fdc8" :answer/id #uuid "2b933277-b836-55ae-9b21-a1a99505fdc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n+1)=2f(n),\\,f(1)=12,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c6698c3-0e55-55e1-a6c5-bc756af04932" :answer/id #uuid "9c6698c3-0e55-55e1-a6c5-bc756af04932" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n+1)=2f(n),\\,f(1)=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71f17afc-b6a1-50e6-8314-cf085641ebf2" :answer/id #uuid "71f17afc-b6a1-50e6-8314-cf085641ebf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n+1)=2f(n),\\,f(1)=6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-227897ea-9dd1-5b96-9c06-008a8a2d99f1" :answer/id #uuid "227897ea-9dd1-5b96-9c06-008a8a2d99f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n+1)=6f(n),\\,f(1)=12,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a562547-fbeb-5f3b-853f-ddb