f a geometric sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nSo, we must determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common ratio $r.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=\\frac{10}{3}.$ To find the common ratio, we compare the given sequence with the general recursive formula for a geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the above, we see that $r=-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{1}=\\frac{10}{3}$ and $r=-\\frac{3}{5}$ into the formula for the $n$th term, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify further by manipulating the exponents as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{-1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10\\cdot 5}{3\\cdot 3}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n} \\\\  & =-\\frac{50}{9}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{50}{9}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-2e69b893-dca1-5a00-a0a1-d673b040380f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-7ee0f6b8-65be-5837-90b0-536ef0f796f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ee0f6b8-65be-5837-90b0-536ef0f796f6"] ["answer-897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" :answer/id #uuid "897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81"] ["answer-897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-897b3115-f689-53ea-8b8f-579dc209df81" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-2\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{5})}^{n},\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" :answer/id #uuid "039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481"] ["answer-039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-039ad15f-aa14-5833-b492-297d15ec8481" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-\\fra